  descriptionChunks:
  - 'The rectum is the final section of the large intestine that stores feces before
    elimination. It plays a key role in waste management and defecation control. '
  - This structure ensures temporary storage and regulates the release of waste from
    the body. Proper function is essential for maintaining digestive health and eliminating
    waste efficiently.
